      "id": "2073400880246796751",
      "text": "since we decided to NOT pay for an expensive marketing email platform (like drip) to create and send from, ive been kinda stuck sending our weekly newsletter as a plain text email from the marketing email studio platform i built with claude code. theres just no way im going to be able to vibe code a high quality email design editor as good as drip for example..already been down that road and burned way too many tokens $$ its not worth it. but now we've established a marketing partnership with a serious local company, and if we're going to mention their name in our newsletter then its time to upgrade the look/feel of our newsletter to be more pretty and professional for our audiences.\n\ni saw a post yesterday that @AnthropicAI just released artifacts on claude code via @ClaudeDevs, which   reminded how well claude builds html artifacts.. which is perfect for email design! so i implemented a new workflow around that... all i had to do was build a \"Compose with HTML\" feature in my email studio platform (one shotted it in 5 mins) so my partner who owns the weekly newsletter can just compose and design the email in claude as an html artifact and copy/paste or import the html into our email studio platform.\n\nour new workflow for sending a high quality designed newsletter email looks like this now (and we still dont have to pay for a SaaS!):",
      "author": {
        "id": "1518360810",
        "name": "randy lunetto",
        "screenName": "randyLunetto",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1952922250828455936/PO9hiHlL_normal.jpg",
        "verified": true
      },
      "metrics": {
        "likes": 2,
        "retweets": 0,
        "replies": 1,
        "quotes": 0,
        "views": 112,
        "bookmarks": 0
